cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AMPER: Adaptive Motor Power and Energy Regulation for FTC"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The Allsparks"
    alias: "FTC Team 36117"
    website: "https://github.com/The-Allsparks"
repository-code: "https://github.com/The-Allsparks/AMPER"
url: "https://github.com/The-Allsparks/AMPER"
abstract: >-
  AMPER is a phased electrical-awareness and power-coordination library for
  FIRST Tech Challenge robots. It begins with passive voltage and current
  instrumentation and progresses through optional reactive and predictive
  power-management phases that remain disabled until validated.
keywords:
  - FIRST Tech Challenge
  - FTC
  - power management
  - brownout prevention
  - battery monitoring
  - robotics
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-SNAPSHOT"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
